# Ignore build outputs from performing a nix-build or `nix build` command
result
result-*

# Ignore automatically generated direnv output
.direnv

# Claude Code writes accepted permission grants here. Its sibling
# .claude/settings.json is tracked (shared config), so the directory is already
# in the repo and this file would otherwise ride along into a repo attendees
# clone.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python track venv (created by `just setup-python`)
.venv/

# --- Language tracks ---
# All tracks are ignored up front, even though Exercise 3 is pick-one:
# trying another language is an extension exercise, and spare ignore
# rules cost nothing. This is the book's "step zero" principle applied —
# which is why the workshop skips the git step: it's already done here.

# Rust
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Rust.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# C build artifacts and shared libraries (every track links against these)
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.out

# Python (venv above)
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Python.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Swift
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Swift.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
.build/
DerivedData/

# Kotlin/JNA (*.jar is ignored as a build output; vendor deps would need an exception)
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Kotlin.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
*.class
*.jar
.gradle/
build/

# Dart
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dart.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
.dart_tool/

# JavaScript / wasm track (Node consumers under days/*/wasm/ and
# exercises/*/wasm/). Only node_modules from the upstream template — the
# rest of Node.gitignore is for apps and publishers, not for a script that
# loads a .wasm. The .wasm itself lives in target/ and is already covered.
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Node.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-09-15
node_modules/
# wasm-bindgen's output directory on the generated lap: the JS glue, the
# renamed _bg.wasm and the .d.ts. Machine output regenerated by
# `just days wasm-demo <day>`, same reasoning as /days/*/include/*.h below —
# and scoped the same way, so any other pkg/ in the tree stays tracked.
/days/*/wasm/pkg/
/exercises/*/wasm/pkg/

# Fortran
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Fortran.gitignore — upstream
# that is a symlink to C++.gitignore, whose object and library rules are the C
# block above. What is Fortran's own: gfortran writes a .mod (and a .smod for a
# submodule) next to every `module` it compiles, the way rustc writes .rmeta —
# machine output, regenerated by every compile. Scoped to the track directory
# because *.mod is also a Go manifest, and jj never warns about an ignored file.
# Pulled: 2026-09-15
**/fortran/*.mod
**/fortran/*.smod
# The compiled consumer, `just days fortran-demo <day>`: an executable with no
# extension, so none of the suffix rules reach it — the same reason
# exercises/.gitignore names ex3-bindings/swift/ex3. `solve` is the name in
# docs/plans; rename here when the recipe lands.
/days/*/fortran/solve

# R
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/R.gitignore (trimmed —
# upstream is written for packages and RStudio projects, and ignores docs/,
# which is a real directory here, so it is not taken wholesale)
# Pulled: 2026-09-15
# `Rscript solve.R` leaves none of these; an interactive R session in the
# track directory leaves all of them.
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.RDataTmp
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
# R CMD build / R CMD check output, if the extendr lap ever becomes a package.
*.Rcheck/
# Not listed: `R CMD SHLIB` writes .o and .so, covered by the C block above.

# Godot
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Godot.gitignore (trimmed —
# no Mono, no translations, no *.tmp; and ~*.dll is already under *.dll above)
# Pulled: 2026-09-15
# The editor's import cache, written the first time a project is opened —
# headless included: `godot --headless -s test.gd` creates .godot/ too.
.godot/
.import/
# Export settings and credentials — credentials are secrets, and there is no
# export in this repo; the rule is here so an accidental one stays out.
export.cfg
export_credentials.cfg
# Not listed: the cdylib the .gdextension descriptor points at is *.so, *.dylib
# or *.dll wherever the demo copies it, and those rules are above. The
# descriptor itself and project.godot are source and stay tracked.

